# Paths exempt from the GENERIC secret scanners in .githooks/pre-commit.
#
# One shell glob per line, matched against the repo-relative path.
#
# This exists for SEC-7: the estate deliberately contains credential-shaped
# synthetic values, and those fixtures would otherwise block every commit.
#
# What this file can never exempt:
#   - flag values (BTA{...})
#   - the fixture manifest
# Both are checked before the allowlist is consulted, and neither is
# overridable. If one is blocking a commit, the value is the problem.
#
# Keep entries narrow. A glob wide enough to cover a whole tree defeats the
# control it is carving an exception out of.

